+# S5-CLM-00003486 frontier
+
+The frozen proposition is the `Claim` polarity
+
+`∀ (S₀ : List ℤ), S₀ ≠ [] → ∃ m, k (S S₀ m) = 1`.
+
+The source record calls this the Curling Number Conjecture and marks it
+research-open.  The target-local statement file preserves the source `k` and
+`S` definitions and proves only `claim_iff_source`; it does not manufacture a
+global theorem.
+
+## Typed frontier
+
+| node | kind | exact obligation | current evidence | cut |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `STMT-EXACT-001` | statement binding | elaborate the exact universal proposition | `Statement.lean`, `claim_iff_source` | none for transport |
+| `LEM-SINGLETON-001` | special case | `∀ a, k [a] = 1` | compiled in `Proof.lean` | does not cover longer seeds |
+| `LEM-SEQUENCE-001` | invariant | nonempty seeds stay nonempty | compiled in `Proof.lean` | does not force a one step |
+| `EXP-FINITE-001` | exploration | bounded enumerations reach 1 | `attempt-001.json` | finite-to-infinite cut |
+| `RES-ROOT-OPEN` | exact root | prove `Claim` or prove `Not Claim` | absent by design | mapping, human, machine, readable |
+
+The four cuts are independent. In particular, the finite enumerator uses an
+ordinary exact-suffix implementation only inside its declared finite boundary;
+it is not a definition of `k` and cannot be promoted to a theorem about all
+integer lists.
+
+## Proof route candidates
+
+1. Establish a structural descent for a persistent curling number greater than
+   one, while respecting the supremum definition of `k`.
+2. Prove that the recurrence cannot maintain a repeated suffix forever, perhaps
+   by a combinatorial invariant on the appended positive integers.
+3. Translate the resulting unbounded existence argument to the exact Lean
+   definitions, with no fixed computational bound.
+
+## Refutation route candidates
+
+1. Exhibit a specific nonempty integer list.
+2. Prove that every iterate has curling number different from one (or otherwise
+   derive the negation of the existential).
+3. Check the witness-to-negation bridge in Lean and place it at the exact
+   `Not Claim` root.
+
+No route is closed in this handoff. The package is therefore an accepted
+exploration handoff, not a resolution or release acceptance.
