+# Resolution outline
+
+This is a route map, not a completed proof.
+
+## Exact root
+
+`R0` is `Arxiv.«0912.2382».Claim`, with polarity `Claim` and statement digest
+`d94e853496a8896d2ff7cdf629410af587acd379551ff3a8a9b0ca72f2474032`.
+
+## Candidate proof route
+
+* `P1` formalize basic suffix-repetition facts for the supremum definition of
+  `k`.
+* `P2` show that if all current curling numbers exceed one, the recurrence
+  creates a strictly controlled combinatorial configuration.
+* `P3` prove that configuration cannot persist for every iterate of an
+  arbitrary nonempty seed.
+* `P4` extract the existential index `m` and check the exact Lean root.
+
+The current singleton lemma is a checked instance of `P1`/`P4`, not `P3`.
+
+## Candidate refutation route
+
+* `N1` search for a concrete seed outside the finite regimes already sampled.
+* `N2` prove a persistent non-one invariant for that seed.
+* `N3` package the invariant as `Not Claim` with a witness-to-negation bridge.
+
+No candidate witness survived the bounded searches, and no `N2` invariant is
+available.
+
+## Required gates
+
+An accepted result needs an exact human argument, a placeholder-free theorem at
+the exact polarity, a reviewed immutable DAG, injective readable anchors, and
+cold offline replay. Until then the four cut IDs in the frontier remain open.
