+# Full target-local study
+
+## 1. Identity and source
+
+This study concerns only `S5CON-00003486-TARGET--worker` and the mathematical
+object `S5-CLM-00003486`. The frozen source is
+`FormalConjectures/Arxiv/0912.2382/CurlingNumberConjecture.lean`, revision
+`2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669`, declaration
+`Arxiv.«0912.2382».curling_number_conjecture`. Its exact proposition is
+
+`(S₀ : List ℤ) (h : S₀ ≠ []) : ∃ m, k (S S₀ m) = 1`.
+
+The source record is classified research-open and contains a placeholder proof.
+The target package does not treat that placeholder as evidence.
+
+## 2. Definitions
+
+`k T` is the natural-number supremum of repetition counts for a nonempty block
+whose repeated flattening is a suffix of `T`. `S S₀ 0 = S₀`, and the successor
+step appends the integer coercion of `k (S S₀ n)`. These definitions are copied
+without a bounded surrogate in `Statement.lean`.
+
+## 3. Exact transport
+
+`SourceStatement` makes all source binders explicit and `Claim` is definitionally
+equal to it. `claim_iff_source` is `Iff.rfl`. The crosswalk records the source
+declaration text, formal-type digest, locator bytes, and mutation rejections.
+
+## 4. Checked mathematics
+
+The proof module establishes that a singleton list has no suffix repetition
+count greater than one and does have count one. It also establishes that the
+recurrence preserves nonemptiness. Therefore every singleton seed reaches the
+target value at index zero. These are exact Lean lemmas and useful sanity
+anchors, but they leave all seeds of length at least two unresolved.
+
+## 5. Exploration
+
+The first bounded run enumerated all 780 seeds over the alphabet
+`{-2,-1,0,1,2}` with lengths 1 through 4 and a 1000-step limit. The second
+checked 399 seeds over `{-3,…,3}` with lengths 1 through 3 and 510 binary seeds
+with lengths 1 through 8, each with a 200-step limit. All 1,689 samples reached
+curling number one. Exact stdout and digests are in `attempt-001.json`.
+
+The finite routine is useful for detecting simple counterexamples and choosing
+proof lemmas. It cannot establish a universal statement over arbitrary integer
+lists, and its implementation is not substituted for the source `sSup`.
+
+## 6. Proof/refutation frontier
+
+The most promising proof direction is a combinatorial persistence obstruction:
+assume `k (S S₀ n) > 1` forever, analyze the repeated suffix blocks, and derive
+a contradiction from the append recurrence. This requires a lemma strong enough
+to handle changing block lengths and the natural supremum. The refutation
+direction requires a seed and an invariant that survives every successor step;
+bounded computation supplied neither.
+
+## 7. Resolution and machine state
+
+Resolution proof units version 1 is a candidate open DAG rooted at
+`RES-ROOT-OPEN`. Its mapping, candidate-human, candidate-machine, and
+readability cuts are nonempty. Lean trust-0 replay checks the local modules and
+special cases, while intentionally declaring no global theorem. Thus human,
+machine, readable, and release debts remain outstanding.
+
+## 8. Reproducibility and invalidation
+
+The package records exact source and baseline digests, commands, outputs,
+artifact hashes, and the frozen self-test command. A change in the source
+fingerprint, proposition, polarity, recurrence, finite scope, toolchain, or
+Stage6 alias invalidates this handoff. A future result must remain under this
+same TARGET claim, use a strictly higher resolution version, and preserve the
+old candidate bytes in the controller archive.
+
+## 9. Handoff conclusion
+
+The worker has completed a truthful exploration and audit package. It has not
+resolved the Curling Number Conjecture. Canonical Master review is required, and
+the TARGET must remain unfinished while any cut remains open.
